Absolutely — with an 8‑week timeline, the smartest approach is to break the project into **phases** that build on each other without overwhelming you. Below is a structured, realistic, production‑style plan that gets your meal‑prep ordering system fully built, tested, and ready to present.

I’ll keep it clear, actionable, and paced so you can actually finish it.

---

# 🗂️ **8‑Week Project Plan — Meal Prep Ordering System**

## 🟦 **Week 1 — Planning & Foundations**
**Goal:** Establish the project structure, requirements, and basic environment.

- Finalise feature list (meal categories, customisation, allergies, tracking, email).
- Finalise tech stack (HTML, CSS, Python Flask, JSON).
- Create the full folder structure in VS Code.
- Set up virtual environment + install Flask.
- Create basic Flask routes (`/`, `/meals`, `/meal/<id>`, `/checkout`, `/track`).
- Create placeholder HTML pages for each route.
- Create initial JSON files:
  - `meals.json`
  - `categories.json`
  - `allergies.json`
  - `drivers.json`
  - `orders.json` (empty)

---

## 🟩 **Week 2 — UI Mockups & Frontend Structure**
**Goal:** Build the visual skeleton of the app.

- Build homepage layout (hero section, categories, featured meals).
- Build meal listing page layout.
- Build meal detail/customisation page layout.
- Build checkout page layout.
- Build tracking page layout.
- Add CSS structure (global styles, components, layout grid).
- Add placeholder images and icons.
- Implement navigation bar + footer.

---

## 🟧 **Week 3 — JSON Data Integration**
**Goal:** Connect frontend pages to real data.

- Load categories from `categories.json`.
- Load meals from `meals.json`.
- Display meals dynamically on category pages.
- Display meal details dynamically on the customisation page.
- Implement allergy filtering (frontend only).
- Implement ingredient removal UI (checkboxes).

---

## 🟨 **Week 4 — Backend Logic (Orders & Customisation)**
**Goal:** Make the app functional.

- Build order object structure in Python.
- Implement ingredient removal logic in backend.
- Implement allergy validation in backend.
- Implement price + calorie recalculation.
- Implement “Add to Cart” functionality (session‑based).
- Build checkout form + validation.
- Save orders to `orders.json`.

---

## 🟪 **Week 5 — Email System & Tracking**
**Goal:** Add communication + tracking features.

- Implement email sending (SMTP or SendGrid).
- Create email template (order summary + tracking link).
- Build tracking route `/track/<order_id>`.
- Display:
  - Order status
  - ETA
  - Driver info
- Implement simulated status updates (e.g., change every 5 minutes).
- Add frontend polling (JavaScript fetch every 10 seconds).

---

## 🟥 **Week 6 — Polish the UI & Add Interactivity**
**Goal:** Make the app feel professional.

- Add animations, hover effects, transitions.
- Improve mobile responsiveness.
- Add loading indicators.
- Add error messages + success messages.
- Add form validation (frontend).
- Add “meal not found” and “order not found” pages.
- Improve card layouts and typography.

---

## 🟫 **Week 7 — Testing, Debugging & Optimisation**
**Goal:** Make sure everything works smoothly.

- Test all routes.
- Test all JSON reads/writes.
- Test email sending.
- Test tracking updates.
- Test allergy filtering.
- Test ingredient removal.
- Fix UI bugs.
- Improve performance (minify CSS/JS).
- Add basic security (input sanitisation).

---

## ⬛ **Week 8 — Finalisation & Presentation**
**Goal:** Prepare the project for submission or demo.

- Write documentation (README, setup instructions).
- Create screenshots of UI.
- Prepare a demo video or live walkthrough.
- Clean up code formatting.
- Add comments to Python + JS files.
- Final review of all pages.
- Package the project for submission.

---

# ⭐ **Optional Enhancements (If Time Allows)**
- Add user accounts + login system.
- Add payment integration (Stripe sandbox).
- Add weekly rotating menus.
- Add real GPS tracking (Google Maps API).
- Add AI meal recommendations.

